# Vulnerability details

## Impact

The `disableHooksTemplate` function from `HooksFactory` sets the `enabled` member of the `HooksTemplate` structure to false. This variable is used to restrict access to the `_deployHooksInstance` function, which is called by `deployHooksInstance` and `deployMarketAndHooks`. Once disabled, a template can never be enabled or added again.
Therefore, a hook can either be enabled or permanently removed.
If `ArchControllerOwner` wants to re-enable this template, he won't be able to use `addHooksTemplate` (the only function that turns `enabled` to true) because it will revert with `HooksTemplateAlreadyExists` (and it shouldn't allow adding that hook because it will override the hook for already deployed markets).


